  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "One computer",
      "items": [
        "./start.sh runs the bridge in Docker with --net=host; Omi Assist and the Desk Guardian start beside it from the same launch file, waiting until the setup page or a flag starts them (start.sh 118–120, phone.launch.py 33–39).",
        "The phone is on the PC's USB: scripts/usb.sh sets adb reverse, so its page is localhost:8782, a secure page for camera, motion and microphone, and the cable charges it (usb.sh 11–16).",
        "The same adb server lets the setup page's phone card look at the phone's load (phone_health.py 21–23)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "Pages and docs",
      "items": [
        "The setup page, on the PC, polls /api/state four times a second; /api answers loopback only (setup.js 322–334, wsserver.py 343–352). Its How it works view is static text (how.js).",
        "The bridge also serves this architecture pack at /docs/; the image carries docs/architecture/*.html (wsserver.py 277–285, Dockerfile 17).",
        "After a restart, the pages reload themselves: the bridge sends its pages' fingerprint on each hello (bridge_node.py 333, face.js 487–491)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Webots beside it",
      "items": [
        "The phone's twin follows the real phone as a mirror, beside atl-bot-thymio's Thymio twin; when the bridge restarts it shows the phone away and joins again every 2 s (atl_phone_twin.py 820–834).",
        "A real Thymio, when connected, is atl-bot-thymio's link on the same ROS domain (guardian_node.py 7–9)."
      ]
    }
  ]
